      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $x+5≡11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The addition property of congruences states that\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a+c≡b+c\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the subtraction property states that\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a-c≡b-c\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe use the subtraction property to subtract $5$ from both sides of the given congruence, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & ≡11\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ x+5-5 & ≡11-5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ x & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
